WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.930
- We are back.
(audience claps)

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.870
And when our next guest discovered
her son's drawing talent,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.610
she wanted to foster that gift.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.140
But, as she quickly realized,

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.930
access to the arts often
falls through the cracks.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:11.040
So, she took action,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.170
and now she's running
a thriving arts program

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.390
for all the kids in her
community, not just her son,

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.981
which is amazing, and that's
why we call her a rad human.

00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:21.481
("Rad Human" theme music)

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.920
All right, everybody, from
Brooklyn's Red Hook Art Project,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.495
also known as RAP, everybody
say hello to Tiffany.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:31.530
(audience cheers)

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.760
So, we were.
- Hi, Kelly!

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.694
- Hello.
- How are you? Hi everyone.

00:00:35.694 --> 00:00:38.070
- So, we were talking about your son.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.770
You noticed he had, you know,
it was very talented art,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.450
but you didn't really know
what to do with that, right?

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:43.590
- No.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.260
- I mean, my children
were always into the arts,

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.800
but as a young mom, giving
birth at the age of 14 years old

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.320
and not having access to the arts myself,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.580
I just didn't understand.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:54.997
For me, it was like,

00:00:54.997 --> 00:00:55.830
"Son, daughter,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.320
you need to know how to
read and do writing."

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.790
I didn't understand the whole.
- The basics.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:03.261
- The basics. I just didn't,
it didn't resonate with me.

00:01:03.261 --> 00:01:06.330
I just didn't, it wasn't until, you know,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.920
he drawing on the walls.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.260
I was like, "somebody's
trying to tell me something.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.737
What do I need to do?"
- Yeah.

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:13.320
"And, first of all,
don't draw on my wall."

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.543
- Exactly. That part.
(audience laughs)

00:01:15.543 --> 00:01:17.418
- But, art classes
weren't an option, right?

00:01:17.418 --> 00:01:19.741
- No, art classes wasn't an option for me.

00:01:19.741 --> 00:01:22.770
You know, living in
low income communities,

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:26.850
going to low income schools,
DOE making a lot of cuts,

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.780
funding, the first thing
they do is pull the arts.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.437
- [Kelly] Arts, yeah.

00:01:30.437 --> 00:01:31.560
- And, for me, that's another
way to silence a child,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.120
another way of silencing a person

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.740
when they don't have
access to these things.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:35.790
Some people are introverts,

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.380
they don't like to speak out loud, right?

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.880
- Yeah.
- So, they like to draw,

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.330
and paint a picture around
what they're trying to say,

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.163
you know?

00:01:43.163 --> 00:01:46.890
So not having access to that
felt like death in itself.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:47.723
- Yeah, no,

00:01:47.723 --> 00:01:50.430
Arts is literally the reason
why I graduated high school,

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:51.720
'cause I had to make certain average

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.795
to be able to participate
in the art program.

00:01:53.795 --> 00:01:54.916
- [Rad Human] Absolutely.

00:01:54.916 --> 00:01:56.280
- So that was what really drove me,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.399
'cause all of our brains
work differently, you know,

00:01:58.399 --> 00:01:59.273
and how we learn.

00:01:59.273 --> 00:02:00.798
So, where is Red Hook Art Project today?

00:02:00.798 --> 00:02:03.299
- Right now, Red Hook
Art Project is an asset

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:06.390
in our community. We do a lot
of work in our communities.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.720
We support students with
building art and music portfolios

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.760
so they can audition for
specialized high schools

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.470
and colleges.
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.930
- We also fight food
insecurities, you know,

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:16.950
just during the pandemic

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.290
we were able to put community
refrigerators outdoors,

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:22.500
and bring over like $1.2
million into the neighborhood

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.019
to make sure kids have access
to food, and also, I mean.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:26.843
- [Kelly] (claps)God, wow.
- For art classes.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.019
- That's incredible.
- Yeah.

00:02:30.019 --> 00:02:32.610
- You're a great mama.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.890
You're like a mama bear
taking care of all the kids.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.240
- Yeah. It's important.
- Yeah.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.950
- So, creative writing programs,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.090
y'all do that as well, right?
- Yes.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.797
Creative writing is a
huge part of our program,

00:02:40.797 --> 00:02:43.650
because again, you can't make art,

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.501
and not be able to express
what it's about, right?

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.790
When you're curating your own art shows,

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.950
you have to be able to write about it,

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.200
write your descriptions,
write your medium.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.850
You know, just write what it's about.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.230
So, I think even in school,

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.510
when you're writing out your
essays to go to college,

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.300
you have to be able to do
creative writing, right?

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.133
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.660
- To be able to get these
scholarships and get these grants.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.277
So, writing is a big part of what we do,

00:03:05.277 --> 00:03:07.200
and it's songwriting.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.170
Like, my daughter, she blossomed
through the organization

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.301
because she used music
and writing as a tool.

00:03:12.301 --> 00:03:13.590
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:15.330
- She graduated high school a year early,

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.260
and show her the tour,

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.730
and then went into cosmetology school.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.780
- Whoa! Oh God.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.540
- All because of her being
able to write and see herself.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:22.863
- Honestly, that was me as a kid as well.

00:03:22.863 --> 00:03:25.770
As soon as I started writing, and music,

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:26.603
it was therapeutic,

00:03:26.603 --> 00:03:28.110
and it gave me a certain
level of confidence

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.220
that I could achieve anything.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.390
I think I believe in that as well.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.670
So, what do you feel like
your organization's impact

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.080
has been on the community?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.000
- Our impact is ensuring that
students have a safe, vibrant

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.960
space to be, they have a voice,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.390
that we meet each of
them where they're at,

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.780
and they have access.
The impact is access.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.176
A lot of us, myself growing
up, didn't have that,

00:03:49.176 --> 00:03:52.560
or didn't even understand
what access or resource meant.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.200
So, I think the impact is
meeting people where they're at

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.060
and giving them that
access that they deserve.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.710
We all want the same thing.
- [Kelly] Opportunity.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:01.200
- Opportunities, and a safe place to be.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.859
- Yeah. You want to be
successful, whatever that means.

00:04:03.859 --> 00:04:04.890
- Absolutely.
- For you and your children.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:08.160
Yeah, absolutely. Well, we
love your passion for the kids.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.170
Like, not just your kids,
but like other kids.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.237
That's incredible. That's
what makes you so rad.

00:04:12.237 --> 00:04:14.550
Red Hook, and for the arts,

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.110
we love what y'all are doing
for the arts in general,

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.300
and so does our season
long partner Pilot Pen,

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.010
makers of friction the
go-to reasonable pen

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:20.970
of the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.460
And, they want to celebrate
those creating fearlessly

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.497
just like you, so they're
gonna give Red Hook Art Project

00:04:26.497 --> 00:04:27.939
$5,000.
- Wow.

00:04:27.939 --> 00:04:30.772
(audience cheers)

00:04:31.657 --> 00:04:32.490
- And, I think it's so
important what you're doing.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:38.010
And, I am from a similar neighborhood,

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.930
like, before I moved,
like, even to Burleson,

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.700
like, I'm from Fort Worth, Texas as well.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:43.357
And, I'm from the same neighborhood.

00:04:43.357 --> 00:04:44.190
We did not have opportunity as well.

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:46.200
So, I now have the means to
help out kids that were me.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.970
So, I'm gonna give you $5,000
as well, so that's 10,000,

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:52.157
because this is helping
out me as a kid too.

00:04:52.157 --> 00:04:54.136
I think it's really
cool what you're doing.

00:04:54.136 --> 00:04:57.459
It's really special, and
setting them up for success

00:04:57.459 --> 00:05:00.036
to give them that edge is amazing.

